],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1792502621,"sha":"ae9629ecd69c9227c314cb9d0e6c5d65a892efd9","subject":"docs(task-relations): add task-relations contract page and wire relation lines"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"45f019003edeaa73a621c7d27a19c698978be9874532a1e3ad47dc0f8172e9b2","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1/chat.md","size_bytes":3882},"commits":{"digest":"5286217a1cb7797330335f2d254a33996456b947c06ef70eff9644e45edbe9b1","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1/commits.json","size_bytes":256},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"3942241a63c5de53df93bede886ed35a51f8b6a33d5883d819c898d7dd34f408","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":83},"meta":{"digest":"5c471296deecc7444d72d4d0bdd536dc17c6d8be60acadc0272d5012d1a98a2a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1/meta.json","size_bytes":14057},"prompt":{"digest":"5dd74c9d0775972bef89b9f16f5c091e8d27e42fd54f8c214eb9b45cb2d08d98","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":184},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"ec49abc41107a402c3c27472a302318e1e81d8d6d7be97931f567213dcc93b4c","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":6949},"state":{"digest":"befc4bbcca49cb87a99e83c67ee0b34a9301acebf900fa140e37a7fbd823884b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-10-20T13:25:21.317613+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.1","local_name":"bob-cli-a2.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-a2","agent_clan_generation":"20261020091040","bead_id":"bob-cli-a2.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-a2[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Task relations: 🪢 LINKS, a generated 🪢 LINKED FROM mirror, and ~ [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]/ ~~ capture[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Bryan can relate any task to any other task with an optional label,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]from Bob Mac Capture (`~` / `~~`) and from the Obsidian Task Card [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](`l` / `⇧L`). The relation is authored once on the source's `🪢 [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]**LINKS:**` line, and a generated `🪢 **LINKED FROM:**` line on the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]target always converges to it. Live chips render both ends [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]correctly, and relations never block, promote, consume, schedule, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]stamp, or route anything.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]15[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_relations.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/task_relations.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-a2[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-a2/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task-relation contract, capture grammar, wire names, and [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]vectors[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: write docs/task-relations.md (grammar, slot, identity, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projection, inertness, invariants, writers, gestures, chips, kill [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]switch, outputs, and every vector table). Add the registry and MC rows [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in task-dependencies.md, the `~` / `~~` capture sections and wire names,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-syntax rows, vault-format, task-status-hooks, and configuration.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Docs only.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust relation grammar, planners, label rules, registry guards,[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]and config[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-core: add src/native/task_relations/ (LINKS and LINKED FROM parsers,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]label normalisation, formatters, canonical sort, slot rules, and edit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planners pinned by LK/LW). Add an is_managed_link_line registry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]predicate at every Task Link guard site, the relations.linked_from_lines[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]config, and MC tests. No writer emits lines yet.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plugin recognisers and gesture guards for relation lines[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plugin-guards[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin-guards: add LK recognisers to nav, the cycler, block-id-prompt, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the ledger plan budget. Keep relation lines out of Task Link, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Pomodoro, tree-close, strike, `!`, and Ctrl+Shift+Enter paths. Give [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Ctrl+Enter and Alt+] parity with dependency lines. Add the LINKED FROM [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hand-edit notice and keep relation lines intact through project [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]conversion. Deploy before any writer.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile owns the LINKED FROM projection[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-reconcile[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-core, plugin-guards[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-reconcile: collect relation edges from active notes, plus read-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]previous daily and done/ sources. Add a reconcile_relation_lines pass [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that inserts, rewrites, deletes, and dedupes LINKED FROM lines, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mints source ids, with guarded output, never pruning on uncertainty, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the kill switch. Add JSON and human outputs, relation_warnings, LR [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests, and a read-only live dry run.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture `~` / `~~` lexer, guards, and capture-parse wire[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-parse[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-parse: add a relation scanner in the `&` / `*` modifier runs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with the digit, slash, strike, escape, and placement guards; labels [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]after `|`; relation_* spans; relations[]; relation_target and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]relation_label needs; owner reuse; the relation_grammar signal; and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]temporary execution refusal. Pinned by LP vectors.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Relation completion pools, label suggestions, and task-id [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]replacements[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-complete[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capture-parse[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-complete: add contexts relation_to, relation_from, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]relation_label; reuse the `&` catalog (open, closed, archived) with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]direction-specific eligibility, ranking, and badges. Label suggestions [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]come from every LINKS line, and a typed-label row returns bob's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]canonical spelling. Add the relation_to_replacement and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]relation_from_replacement task-id fields, the owner-picker relations[], [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and shell groups.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Execute `~` / `~~` captures with a same-batch mirror[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-execute[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capture-parse, plugin-guards[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-execute: plan relations for new and existing owners in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]staged batch. Append or relabel the source's LINKS line, mint the ids [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the edge needs, and stage the target's LINKED FROM through the cli-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]delta planner. Add refusals, inertness, relation_updates, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]linked_from_line_updates, task blocks, human output, and dry-run parity.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Remove the parse-phase refusal. Pinned by LX vectors.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-ledger-tools live relation index and api.relationIndex[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]relation-index[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plugin-guards[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]relation-index: build a raw-text relation index in bob-ledger-tools. It [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]does a prefiltered startup scan including done/, reparses per file on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]change, delete, and rename, overlays unsaved editor text, publishes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]forward and reverse maps together, and resolves targets by path plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]block id. Publish it as api.relationIndex v1 with label suggestions. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Measure cold and warm costs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]nav relation grammar twin, planner, mint, writer, and [/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]api.relations[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-writer[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plugin-guards[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-writer: add the JS twin of the LINKS / LINKED FROM planners (LW and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]LM bytes equal to Rust) and applyRelationEdit. It writes one same-note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]transaction, mints inside the source's transaction, and sends cross-note[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mirror follow-ups with an honest failure suffix. Add the kill switch, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notices, a machine-write annotation, and nav api.relations (removeLink [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]now, openStage once the stages land, v1 after both). No UI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-ledger-tools LINKS and LINKED FROM chips[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]chips[dim] · [dim][/dim]after relation-index[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chips: render live chips for both relation rows in Live Preview and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Reading view from the index, never the stored mirror. Add label pills, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inverse phrases, ✓×N collapse, dashed stale and broken chips, and ＋ / ×[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]controls through nav api.relations. Reuse the bob-dep chip family with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]no new palette, and add LC tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task Card `l` Links to… and the Links stage with the relation[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]field[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-links-stage[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-writer, relation-index[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-links-stage: add the Task Card row `l` and Ctrl+Shift+L, the Links [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stage (open, closed, then archived pool; CURRENT, RESULTS, and CLOSED), [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]↵ link and ⇧↵ link with a relation, CURRENT unlink and relabel, Tab [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]marks, ID prompts, the consequence strip, and Ctrl+Shift+P on a LINKS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]line opening the owner's stage.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task Card `⇧L` Linked from…, counted gestures, hand-edit [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]mirror, and Ctrl+D[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-linked-from[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-links-stage[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-linked-from: add the reverse stage (⇧L, Ctrl+Shift+Alt+L, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Ctrl+Shift+P on a LINKED FROM line) that writes other tasks' LINKS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lines, counted N<Ctrl+Shift+L> sources, and the LINKS hand-edit mirror [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with undo re-arm. Ctrl+D on the Links to row removes every link, Ctrl+D [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on Linked from is refused, and LG vectors are tested.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture `~` / `~~` pickers, live flip, and spans[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-picker[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capture-complete[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-picker: give the direction-aware picker String sigils (& * ~ ~~), [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the relation picker sources, the live flip when a second `~` is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]typed, relation span colours (a new knot accent), the Add-ID flow using [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob's relation replacements, and real-bob fixtures, with portable-check [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and a macOS typecheck.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  14 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture relation card, preview rows, and capability [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]warning[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-preview[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mac-picker, capture-execute[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-preview: add the ⇧↩ relation card (field, suggestion chips with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]counts, live sentence, and bob's inserted token), the 🪢 preview rows [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from relation_updates, managed-line suppression, the relation_grammar [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capability warning, docs, and fixtures. Verify on macOS CI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  15 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Install, pilot on a vault copy, reach the MacBook, guide, and[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]memory[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-reconcile, capture-execute, chips, nav-linked-from, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]mac-preview[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollout: install bob and the plugins on athena, then check that the live[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconcile dry run shows zero relation changes. Run the pilot script on a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault copy, update the MacBook best-effort, write the user guide, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the memory records the accepted decisions allow, and record what is left[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for Bryan.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-a2","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-a2.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-c1cc700fb1ca223a6824e833aac80c60","started_at":"2026-10-20T13:12:02.068066+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"7db0afbab257dc4411aabb7cf0dd0e06d4915890ca33527b9fb9e125c234ea98","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.6/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"ea89d3c191f8c77ebbd62b64aa00c2512b5b4ce073bb9aed3f08e045e4e12deb","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.6/meta.json","size_bytes":688},"prompt":{"digest":"f64ef34e1a73aa2c9b442ef5f3a46a4580290b352e2df1fd74bbde7aa8d28324","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-a2.6/prompt.md","size_bytes":176},"state":{"digest"